 "_note": "Player names read by eye from the leaderboard screenshots, for rows where no other source could supply one. Highest precedence in export_captures: this file, then the rank popup's name, then the leaderboard OCR.",
 "_why": "Names read by eye from the leaderboard screenshots. Highest precedence in export_captures: this file, then the rank popup's name, then the leaderboard OCR.\nTwo groups are here. The first is rows no automatic reader could supply at all. The second is rows where Tesseract produced something that LOOKED like a name and was therefore believed -- the installed Tesseract has only the 'eng' model, so it cannot render Turkish, Cyrillic, Greek or CJK at all and substitutes Latin letters that pass every plausibility check. 'ISAK' was really CJK; 'BENZE' was spaced capitals; 'syOpamies' was Finnish with umlauts. Nothing mechanical can catch that, because the wrong answer is a well-formed word.",
 "_truncated": "A name ending in '...' is truncated BY THE GAME. The leaderboard row clips long names and there is no wider render of them to read, so the ellipsis is what the player's name looks like in this UI, not a reading failure.",
